  "last_message": "I reverted the change before committing anything. `docs/features/reminders.md` documents that the pantry already tried email (April\u2013June 2025) specifically to cut SMS costs, and reverted it after: 34% of reminders went unopened, missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of orders, and volunteers had to throw away uncollected fresh food. There's also an ADR (`docs/adr/0002-send-sms-through-one-provider.md`) and a runbook (`docs/runbooks/sms-provider-down.md`) built around SMS being the channel.\n\nSwitching back to email risks repeating that exact outcome. Do you still want to proceed, or would you rather look at other ways to cut the \u20ac40/month SMS cost (e.g. a cheaper provider, consolidating sends)?",
